<article class="env-lemma" id="06LC">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06LC">Lemma <span data-tag="06LC">10.104.10</span>.</a> Let $\varphi : A \to B$ be a map of local rings. Assume that $B$ is Noetherian and Cohen-Macaulay and that $\mathfrak m_ B = \sqrt{\varphi (\mathfrak m_ A) B}$. Then there exists a sequence of elements $f_1, \ldots , f_{\dim (B)}$ in $A$ such that $\varphi (f_1), \ldots , \varphi (f_{\dim (B)})$ is a regular sequence in $B$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By induction on $\dim (B)$ it suffices to prove: If $\dim (B) \geq 1$, then we can find an element $f$ of $A$ which maps to a nonzerodivisor in $B$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/02JN" data-tag="02JN">10.104.2</a> it suffices to find $f \in A$ whose image in $B$ is not contained in any of the finitely many minimal primes $\mathfrak q_1, \ldots , \mathfrak q_ r$ of $B$. By the assumption that $\mathfrak m_ B = \sqrt{\varphi (\mathfrak m_ A) B}$ we see that $\mathfrak m_ A \not\subset \varphi ^{-1}(\mathfrak q_ i)$. Hence we can find $f$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/00DS" data-tag="00DS">10.15.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>